ROCKNIX: keep "Initramfs unpacking failed" off the console

KERN_EMERG prints on every console, over the boot splash. Log it at
KERN_INFO (ROCKNIX uses KERN_DEBUG): off the console at the default
loglevel, but still in the journal's normal priorities if a real
initramfs failure needs looking into.

diff -rupbN linux.orig/init/initramfs.c linux/init/initramfs.c
--- linux.orig/init/initramfs.c	2026-07-28 15:53:35.261634269 +0000
+++ linux/init/initramfs.c	2026-07-28 15:56:55.329082848 +0000
@@ -728,7 +728,7 @@ static void __init do_populate_rootfs(vo
 #ifdef CONFIG_BLK_DEV_RAM
 		populate_initrd_image(err);
 #else
-		printk(KERN_EMERG "Initramfs unpacking failed: %s\n", err);
+		printk(KERN_INFO "Initramfs unpacking failed: %s\n", err);
 #endif
 	}
 
